   SECTION 2.  That all ordinances and resolutions or parts thereof enacted
prior to May 15, 2007, which are inconsistent with any provision of the
Codified Ordinances, are hereby repealed effective 12:01AM Monday, July 2,
2007, except as follows: the enactment of the Codified Ordinances shall not be
construed to affect a right or liability accrued or incurred under any
legislative provision prior to the effective date of such enactment, or an
action or proceeding for the enforcement of such right or liability. Such
enactment shall not be construed to relieve any person from punishment for an
act committed in violation of any such legislation provision, nor to affect an
indictment or prosecution thereof. For such purposes, any such legislative
provision shall continue in full force notwithstanding its repeal for the
purpose of revision and codification.
   SECTION 3. That one book-form copy of the Codified Ordinances shall be
certified as correct by the Council President and the Clerk of Council,
attached to this Ordinance as a part hereof, and filed with the permanent
ordinance records of the City of Mentor, Ohio.
   SECTION 4.    That existing Mentor Code of Ordinances Chapters and
Subsections and specifically Chapter 92 shall remain in effect as necessary and
obvious and the subsequent revised, rearranged and consolidated ordinances
beginning herein on Page 9 Chapter 101 though Page 20 Chapter 1509 shall be
adopted and effective for all offenses, occurrences and applications occurring
on or after 12:01AM on Monday, July 2, 2007. 
SECTION 5. That it is found and determined that all formal actions of this
Council concerning and relating to the passage of this ordinance were adopted
in an open meeting of this Council and that, except as otherwise provided by
Section 121.22 of the Ohio Revised Code, all deliberations of this Council and
of any of its committees that resulted in such formal action were in meetings
open to the public in compliance with all legal requirements.
SECTION 6. That this ordinance is hereby declared to be an emergency measure
necessary for the preservation of the public peace, health, welfare and safety
of the inhabitants of this City and for the further reason that enhancement of
criminal penalties should become effective as soon as possible, but with
sufficient time left after passage of the enabling ordinance to print and
circulate the revisions to officers and other employees. WHEREFORE, this
ordinance shall take effect and be in force from and immediately upon its
passage.
 
/s/ Ray Kirchner                                
   Mayor and President of Council
PASSED: _June 5, 2007______________
 
ATTEST: /s/ Elizabeth A. Limestahl  
      Clerk of Council
 
