105.01 WARDS AND WARD BOUNDARIES.
   The City of Mentor is hereby divided into four wards, the boundaries of
which are as follows:
Ward No. 1:
The first ward shall contain all that territory bounded and described as
follows:
   Beginning at a point in the centerline of State Route 2 (Lakeland Freeway),
and the easterly corporation line of the City of Mentor and the west township
line of Painesville Township;
   Thence running along a centerline and State Route 2 (Lakeland Freeway), in a
southwesterly direction to a point of intersection of the centerline of State
Route 2 (Lakeland Freeway), and the centerline of Munson Road;
   Thence northwesterly along the centerline of Munson Road to a point of
intersection at the centerline of Collins Road;
   Thence southerly along the centerline of Melshore Drive to a point of
intersection at the centerline of Edgewood Drive;
   Thence easterly along the centerline of Edgewood Drive to a point of
intersection at the centerline of State Route 615 (Center Street);
   Thence southerly along the centerline of State Route 615 to a point of
intersection of the centerline of Station Street;
   Thence in an easterly direction along the centerline of Station Street to a
point of intersection of the centerline of Jackson Street;
   Thence southerly along the centerline of Jackson Street and Little Mountain
Road to the southern corporation line of the City of Mentor and the corporation
line of the Village of Kirtland Hills;
   Thence easterly in an irregular pattern along the southerly corporation line
of the City of Mentor and the northerly corporation line of Kirtland Hills
Village to a point where said corporation lines intersect with the Township
line of Concord Township;
   Thence northerly along said corporation line of Concord Township and the
easterly corporation line of the City of Mentor in a due northerly direction to
the point where the Township line of Painesville Township intersects with said
Mentor City corporation line;
   Thence continuing northerly along said corporation lines to the centerline
of State Route 2 (Lakeland Freeway) being the place of beginning.
Ward No. 2:
The second ward shall contain all that territory bounded and described as
follows:
   Beginning at a point in the intersection of the centerline of State Route
615 (Center Street), and the centerline of Edgewood Drive;
   Thence running southerly along the centerline of State Route 615 (Center
Street) in a due southerly direction to a point of intersection of the
centerline of Station Street;
   Thence easterly along the centerline of Station Street to a point of
intersection of the centerline of Jackson Street;
   Thence southerly along the centerline of Jackson Street and Little Mountain
Road to the southerly corporation line of the City of Mentor and the
corporation line of the Village of Kirtland;
   Thence continuing in an irregular pattern along the southerly corporation
line of the City of Mentor and said corporation line of Kirtland City; westerly
to a point where said line intersects an easterly corporation line of the City
of Willoughby, said corporation line being approximately 300 feet southerly
from Interstate 90;
   Thence following an irregular pattern along the southerly corporation line
of Mentor City and the corporation line of the City of Willoughby to a point on
the northerly side of the New York Central Railroad right-of-way;
   Thence northerly continuing along the corporation lines of the City of
Mentor and the City of Willoughby to a point at the intersection at the
centerline of Hodgson Road;
   Thence easterly along the centerline of Hodgson Road to a point of
intersection at the centerline of Culver Boulevard;
   Thence southeasterly along the centerline of Culver Boulevard to a point of
intersection of Farnham Drive;
   Thence easterly along the centerline of Farnham Drive to a point of
intersection with State Route 306;
   Thence southerly along the centerline of State Route 306 to a point on the
centerline of State Route 2 (Lakeland Freeway);
   Thence northeasterly along the centerline of State Route 2 (Lakeland
Freeway) to a point at the intersection of the centerline of State Route 2
(Lakeland Freeway), and the extended northerly property line of Sublot 136 in
the Weatherby Park Subdivision 4A;
   Thence westerly along the said northerly property line of sublot 136 in
Weatherby Park Subdivision 4A to a point of intersection of the westerly
subdivision line of Kingsmill Subdivision Phase 3;
   Thence northerly along the westerly subdivision line of Kingsmill
Subdivision Phase 3 to a point of intersection of the centerline of Bellflower
Road;
   Thence continuing northerly along the centerline of Bellflower Road to a
point of intersection of the centerline of Bellflower Road (section east of
King Arthur Estates Subdivision);
   Thence easterly along the centerline of Bellflower Road to a point of
intersection of the centerline of Elmwood Road;
   Thence in a northerly direction along the centerline of Elmwood Road to a
point of intersection with the centerline of Edgewood Road;
   Thence in an easterly direction along the centerline of Edgewood Road to the
centerline of State Route 615 (Center Street) the place of beginning.
Ward No. 3:
The third ward shall contain all that territory bounded and described as
follows:
   Beginning at a point at the intersection of the centerline of Plains Road
and the centerline of Collins Road;
   Thence southerly along the centerline of Collins Road to a point of
intersection at the centerline of Munson Road;
   Thence westerly along the centerline of Munson Road to a point of
intersection at the centerline of Melshore Drive;
   Thence southerly along the centerline of Melshore Drive to a point of
intersection at the centerline of Edgewood Road;
   Thence westerly along the centerline of Edgewood Road to a point of
intersection at the centerline of Elmwood Road;
   Thence southerly along the centerline of Elmwood Road to a point of
intersection at the centerline of Bellflower Road;
   Thence westerly along the centerline of Bellflower Road to a point of
intersection at the centerline of Bellflower Road (section to the east of King
Arthur Estates Subdivision);
   Thence continuing in a southerly direction along the centerline of
Bellflower Road and the easterly subdivision line of the Kingsmill Subdivision
Phase 3 to a point of intersection of the northerly property line of Sublot 136
in Weatherby Park Subdivision;
   Thence easterly along the northerly property line of sublot 136 Weatherby
Park Subdivision Phase 3 to a point of intersection at the centerline of State
Route 2 (Lakeland Freeway);
   Thence in a southwesterly direction along the centerline of State Route 2
(Lakeland Freeway) to a point of intersection at the centerline of State Route
306 (Reynolds Road);
   Thence northerly along the centerline of State Route 306 (Reynolds Road) to
a point of intersection at the centerline of Farnham Drive;
   Thence westerly along the centerline of Farnham Drive to a point of
intersection at the centerline of Culver Boulevard;
   Thence in a northwesterly direction to a point on the corporation lines of
the City of Mentor and the City of Willoughby;
   Thence in a due northerly direction along said corporation lines of the City
of Mentor and the City of Willoughby to the intersection of the centerline of
State Route 283 (Lake Shore Boulevard);
   Thence continuing north along the centerline of Iroquois Avenue to a point
of intersection of the corporation lines of the City of Mentor and the City of
Mentor-on-the-Lake;
   Thence in an easterly direction along said corporation lines of the City of
Mentor and the City of Mentor-on-the-Lake to a point of intersection at the
centerline of State Route 283 (Lake Shore Boulevard);
   Thence continuing in an easterly direction along the centerline of Lake
Shore Boulevard (State Route 283) to a point where said centerline intersects
with the centerline of Munson Road to a point on the corporation lines of the
City of Mentor and the City of Mentor-on-the- Lake;
   Thence in a northerly direction along said corporation lines of the City of
Mentor and the City of Mentor-on-the Lake to a point of intersection at the
centerline of Plains Road;
   Thence in a northeasterly direction along the centerline of Plains Road to a
point of intersection at the centerline of Collins Road and the place of
beginning.
Ward No. 4:
The fourth ward shall contain all that territory bounded and described as
follow:
   Beginning at a point at the intersection of the centerline of State Route 2
(Lakeland Freeway) and the centerline of Munson Road;
   Thence in a northwesterly direction along said centerline of Munson Road to
a point of intersection at the centerline of Collins Road;
   Thence in a northerly direction along the centerline of Collins Road to a
point where the centerline of Collins Road intersects with the centerline of
Plains Road;
   Thence westerly along the centerline of Plains Road to a point on the
corporation lines of the City of Mentor and the City of Mentor-on-the-Lake;
   Thence northerly and easterly in an irregular pattern along said corporation
lines of the City of Mentor and the City of Mentor-on-the-Lake to the north
corporation line of the City of Mentor at the southern shores of Lake Erie;
   Thence in a northeasterly direction along said north corporation line and
the southern shores of Lake Erie to where said corporation line intersects with
the Township line of Painesville Township;
   Thence in a due southerly direction along the corporation line of the City
of Mentor and the Township line of Painesville Township to a point where said
lines intersect with the corporation line of the Village of Grand River;
   Thence continuing southerly along said corporation lines of the City of
Mentor and the Village of Grand River to a point where said lines intersect
with the Township line of the Township of Painesville;
   Thence continuing southerly along said Township line and the City of Mentor
corporation line to the centerline of State Route 2 (Lakeland Freeway);
   Thence in a southwesterly direction along said centerline of State Route 2
(Lakeland Freeway), to the centerline of Munson Road being the place of
beginning.
(1969 Code 4.01)
