151.01 RESIDENCE REQUIREMENTS.
   Except as otherwise provided by Charter, no full-time or part-time officer
or employee of the City of Mentor is required to be a resident of the City
either at the time of appointment or during the term of employment or such
appointment. (Ord. 07-0-33. Passed 3-20-07.)
151.02 CLASSIFICATION OF POSITIONS.
   All positions in the municipal service shall be grouped into classes and
each class shall include those positions sufficiently similar in respect to
their duties and responsibilities so that similar requirements as to training,
experience, knowledge and skills, and the same rules of compensation are
applicable thereto. (Ord. 07-0-33. Passed 3-20-07.)
151.03 ADOPTION OF CLASSIFICATION PLAN.
   The list of classification titles and the specifications for the respective
classes are hereby adopted and the official copy of such classifications and
specifications shall be filed in the offices of the City Clerk, and shall
include such changes and additions as may be recommended by the City Manager
from time to time and approved by Council.
(Ord. 07-0-33. Passed 3-20-07.)
151.04 PURPOSE AND EFFECT OF CLASSIFICATION SPECIFICATIONS.
   Each class specification outlines the main characteristic and qualification
requirements of positions in the class and gives examples of specific duties
which employees holding such positions may properly be required to perform. The
class specification is descriptive and explanatory but not restrictive. The
listing of particular examples of duties do not preclude the assignment of
other tasks by the department director, division head, or supervisor.
(Ord. 07-0-33. Passed 3-20-07.)
151.05 STATEMENTS OF DESIRABLE QUALIFICATIONS.
   The statement of qualifications in a class specification is intended to be
used as a guide in selecting persons for employment and for use in determining
the relative value of positions in a class with positions in other classes.
(Ord. 07-0-33. Passed 3-20-07.)
151.06 RESPONSIBILITIES OF THE CITY MANAGER.
   The City Manager or his designated agent shall be responsible for the work
of administering and maintaining the classification plan. The City Manager
shall consider and approve necessary reviews and preparation of reports
recommending appropriate actions to assure that the classification plan is kept
current and that any important changes in duties and responsibilities in any
existing positions and new positions, are reflected in the plan, before
submission to the City Council for final action. (Ord. 07-0-33. Passed 3-20-
07.)
151.061 ASSISTANT CLERK OF COUNCIL.
   The Assistant Clerk of Council shall be appointed and removed by majority
vote of the members of Council. The Assistant Clerk of Council shall be the
Recording Secretary for and attend all meetings of the Municipal Planning
Commission and Board of Building and Zoning Appeals. The Assistant Clerk of
Council shall further perform the duties assigned by and work under the general
supervision of the Clerk of Council. During the absence or disability of the
Clerk of Council, the Assistant Clerk of Council shall serve as Acting Clerk of
Council during all such periods of absence or disability. (Ord. 20-O-024.
Passed 3-3-20.)
151.07 PAYMENT FROM FUNDS.
   All officers and employees of the City shall be paid from the fund or funds
allocated to the operations for which their services were performed as
determined by the City Manager.
(Ord. 07-0-33. Passed 3-20-07.)
151.08 COMPENSATION SCHEDULES.
   The rates of pay for city employees shall be based on the appropriate pay
grade prescribed herein for each position as shown in Section
151.16.
(Ord. 07-0-33. Passed 3-20-07.)
151.09 BASIS OF COMPENSATION SCHEDULES.
   All regular full-time employees shall be paid on the schedule of bi-weekly
salaries prescribed herein for their respective position classification, and
designated hourly rate positions shall be paid on the schedule of hourly rates
prescribed therefore. Salaries of temporary or part-time positions shall be
based on hourly rates and/or determined as provided in this chapter. For the
purpose of applying the provisions of the salary ordinances, annual salaries
shall be deemed to be equivalent to the dollar amount divided by 26 pay periods
to produce a bi-weekly rate.
(Ord. 07-0-33. Passed 3-20-07.)
151.10 ADOPTION OF COMPENSATION PLAN.
   The compensation plan is subject to the availability of funds and is hereby
adopted. The compensation plan includes listings of part-time, full-time and
non-classified positions and associated pay grades along with the
classification as exempt or non-exempt from overtime compensation in accordance
with the Fair Labor Standards Act Regulations Title 29 Code of Federal
Regulations.
(Ord. 07-0-33. Passed 3-20-07.)
