151.14 COLLECTIVE BARGAINING UNIT POSITIONS.
   All collective bargaining agreements govern the employees of each bargaining
unit listed below. Copies of all collective bargaining agreements are on file
in the offices of the Clerk of Council and the City Manager.
   (a)   The Ohio Patrolmen’s Benevolent Association (Police Officers)
   (b)   The Ohio Patrolmen’s Benevolent Association (Sergeants and
Lieutenants)
   (c)   The Ohio Patrolmen’s Benevolent Association (Communications
Technicians and Corrections Officers)
   (d)   The Mentor Professional Firefighters Association, International
Association of Firefighters, Local 1845
   (e)   The Mentor Part-Time Firefighters Association
   (f)   Laborers’ International Union of North America, Local Union Number
860, AFL-CIO. (Ord. 23-O-038. Passed 4-18-23.)
151.15 TEMPORARY AND/OR SEASONAL EMPLOYEES.
   (a)   Temporary and/or seasonal employees are to be paid and serve under
such terms and conditions as the City Manager may direct. Temporary and/or
seasonal employees are not regular full-time or regular part-time employees of
the City.
   (b)    Seasonal Employee - A seasonal employee works a certain regular
season and for FLSA purposes is considered exempt from overtime compensation.
   
   (c)   Temporary Employee - A temporary employee is an employee who may work
at any time during the year performing a function or providing a service to
supplement the full- time and regular part-time workforce at various times
throughout the year and for FLSA purposes is considered non-exempt from
overtime compensation.
(Ord. 08-0-01. Passed 2-5-08.)
