155.01 ELECTION OF OFFICERS.
   The Municipal Planning Commission each even numbered year shall have an
organizational meeting during its first meeting of the calendar year. At such
organizational meeting the Commission shall elect a Chairman, Vice-Chairman and
Secretary for a term of two years or until the next organization election is
held pursuant to this section.
(Ord. 10-O-80. Passed 9-7-10.)
155.02 CHAIRMAN.
   The Chairman of the Municipal Planning Commission shall preside at all
meetings of the Commission and shall perform all other ordinary duties of such
an office. The Chairman may represent the Commission before City Council and
the public and shall appoint such committees as are necessary to expedite the
functions of the Commission.
(Ord. 10-O-80. Passed 9-7-10.)
155.03 VICE-CHAIRMAN.
   There shall be a Vice-Chairman to serve in the absence of the Chairman. The
Vice-Chairman shall perform such other duties as are assigned by the Chairman
or the Commission. (Ord. 10-O-80. Passed 9-7-10.)
155.04 SECRETARY.
   There shall be a Secretary who shall preside at meetings in the absence of
both the Chairman and the Vice-Chairman.
(Ord. 10-O-80. Passed 9-7-10.)
155.05 RECORDING SECRETARY.
   The Assistant Clerk of Council or designee shall be the Recording Secretary
and shall keep the minutes of the Commission. Minutes shall be made and
maintained of all proceedings, showing the action of the Commission and the
vote of each member upon each question.
(Ord. 14-O-95. Passed 10-7-14; Ord. 20-O-024. Passed 3-3-20.)
155.06 LEGAL COUNSEL.
   The Assistant Law Director, Zoning Counsel or other member of the Law
Department will attend all meetings of the Commission.
(Ord. 10-O-80. Passed 9-7-10.)
155.07 VACANCY OF OFFICER.
   In the event of a vacancy in the office of Chairman, Vice-Chairman or
Secretary, the Commission shall by majority vote, elect a successor to serve
the remainder of the term; but pending such election, the Vice-Chairman shall
fill the office of Chairman until a new Chairman is elected. (Ord. 10-O-80.
Passed 9-7-10.)
155.08 REGULAR MEETINGS.
   The Municipal Planning Commission shall regularly meet every third Thursday,
commencing from January of each new calendar year, at 7:00 p.m. in the Council
Chambers of the Mentor Municipal Center and at such other times and locations
as the Commission may, by resolution, determine. Notwithstanding the foregoing,
the Commission may meet only once in the month of December and the Commission
may upon motion previously adopted modify the dates of the final two regular
meetings of the calendar year or any other holiday conflicts.
(Ord. 22-O-089. Passed 11-1-22.)
155.09 SPECIAL MEETINGS.
   Special meetings shall be called at the discretion of the Chairman with a
minimum three days notice to the members. Such notice will specify the purpose
for which the meeting is called.
(Ord. 10-O-80. Passed 9-7-10.)
155.10 MEETINGS OPEN TO PUBLIC.
   All regular meetings, special meetings and work sessions of the Commission
shall be open to the public, subject to lawful adjournment into Executive
Session. No final action will be taken at a work session. (Ord. 10-O-80. Passed
9-7-10.)
155.11 MEETING AGENDA.
   The meeting agenda will be provided to the members of the Municipal Planning
Commission no later than Friday of the week prior to the regularly scheduled
meeting.
(Ord. 10-O-80. Passed 9-7-10.)
155.12 AGENDA REQUIREMENTS.
   Applications which are incomplete pursuant to applicable sections of the
Code as of the deadline established for their submission shall not be placed on
the agenda.
(Ord. 10-O-80. Passed 9-7-10.)
155.13 ORDER OF BUSINESS.
   The order of business, unless otherwise waived or amended by vote of the
Commission, shall be as follows:
   (a)   Call to Order.
   (b)   Pledge of Allegiance.
   (c)   Roll Call.
   (d)   Approval of Minutes.
   (e)   Public Hearings.
   (f)   Old Business.
   (g)   New Business.
   (h)   Director’s Report.
   (i)   Adjournment.
      (Ord. 10-O-80. Passed 9-7-10.)
155.14 MEETING TIME RESTRICTIONS.
   Unless otherwise waived by the Commission, all public hearings, new
business, and action on old business will be heard and acted upon before 10:30
p.m.; and no other business will be transacted or discussed after that time.
(Ord. 10-O-80. Passed 9-7-10.)
155.15 QUORUM.
   Four (4) members shall constitute a quorum for the transaction of official
business.
(Ord. 10-O-80. Passed 9-7-10.)
155.16 ABSENCE OF MEMBERS.
   Members of the Commission are responsible for notifying the Chairman or
Recording Secretary of their impending absence from a Commission meeting and
the reason thereof.
(Ord. 10-O-80. Passed 9-7-10.)
155.17 PASSAGE OF MOTIONS.
   Action shall be taken by motion, and a majority affirmative vote is
necessary for the passage of any motion except those rules of procedure
requiring a two-thirds vote and amendments to these rules and regulations.
(Ord. 10-O-80. Passed 9-7-10.)
155.18 ZONING AND LAND USE CHANGE.
   Subject to Section
155.15, if a majority of the members at a meeting of the Municipal Planning
Commission at which a quorum is present vote in favor of recommending a zoning
or land use change or other motion, the same shall be deemed to be a favorable
recommendation. If a majority of the members at a meeting of the Municipal
Planning Commission at which a quorum is present vote against recommending a
zoning of land use change or other motion, or if a tie vote results, the same
shall be deemed to be an unfavorable recommendation.
(Ord. 10-O-80. Passed 9-7-10.)
155.19 MOTION TO RECONSIDER.
   Any action taken by the Commission may be reconsidered by a Motion to
Reconsider made by any member, provided that such action to reconsider take
place prior to the conclusion of the meeting at which the initial action was
taken.
(Ord. 10-O-80. Passed 9-7-10.)
155.20 CHANGES TO ZONING CODE OR SUBDIVISION CODE.
   Text changes to the Zoning Code or the Subdivision Code may be originated by
individual members of the Commission. These proposed text changes will be
included on the Commission agenda upon the request of any two members of the
Commission.
(Ord. 10-O-80. Passed 9-7-10.)
155.21 MINOR SUBDIVISIONS.
   Minor subdivisions approved by the Director of Planning pursuant to Section
1111.05 of Mentor's Code of Ordinances will be reported to the Municipal
Planning Commission, in writing, at the next Commission meeting following
approval; said report will specify as a minimum the applicant's name, location,
size and dimensions of each minor subdivision approved.
(Ord. 10-O-80. Passed 9-7-10; Ord. 18-O-075. Passed 9-4-18.)
155.22 ROLL CALL OR VOTE OF CHAIRMAN.
   For purposes of voting, the Recording Secretary shall call the roll of
members of the Commission in rolling alphabetical order of their last names,
with the Chairman voting last.
(Ord. 10-O-80. Passed 9-7-10.)
155.23 EXPENDITURE OF CITY FUNDS.
   Attendance and designation of Commission members at professional meetings,
seminars, conferences, training workshops, or such other like activity,
involving an expenditure of City funds, shall be approved in advance by the
Commission Chairman and then presented for approval to the President of
Council.
(Ord. 10-O-80. Passed 9-7-10.)
155.24 APPLICANT OR APPELLANT FEES.
   Fees to be charged applicants or appellants, unless otherwise specified,
shall be established by the Director of Planning and the Municipal Planning
Commission will be notified.
(Ord. 10-O-80. Passed 9-7-10; Ord. 18-O-075. Passed 9-4-18.)
155.25 REMOVAL OF MEMBERS.
   (a)   A member of the Municipal Planning Commission may be expelled or
removed from the Commission for one or more of the following reasons:
      (1)   Conviction while in office of a felony or other crime involving
moral turpitude;
      (2)   Violation of his oath of office, including gross misconduct or
malfeasance or nonfeasance in, or disqualification for office.
      (3)   Continuous absence from more than three consecutive regular
meetings of the Municipal Planning Commission without a valid reason or excused
absence by the Chairman or absence from more than fifty percent of the regular
meetings during any twelve-month period.
   (b)   Action to remove a member from the Commission can be brought by two or
more members of the Commission, in writing, specifying the reasons for
requesting removal. A date will be set for a public hearing. The accused member
shall be notified in writing of the charge or charges against him at least
fifteen days in advance of such public hearing; and he or his counsel shall be
given an opportunity to be heard, present evidence, and examine witnesses
appearing in support of such charge or charges.
   (c)   Expulsion or removal from the Commission shall be upon the concurrence
of five or more members of the Municipal Planning Commission after a public
hearing upon the charge or charges brought and thereupon the office of any such
removed or expelled member of the Commission shall be vacant. The City Council
will be notified of the vacancy on the Commission so that a replacement member
can be appointed.
(Ord. 10-O-80. Passed 9-7-10.)
155.26 MATERIALS FOR BROADCAST.
   All persons desiring to publish photos, renderings, exhibits, electronic
presentations, or any other media during any broadcast Commission meeting
(including both telecast and internet) shall provide to the Department of
Planning and Development full and complete copies of same no later than the
Friday previous to the meeting (or Monday, if any Friday is a public holiday).
Failure to do so shall result in the exclusion of any such items from being
shown publicly during the course of the broadcast meeting.
   The Department of Planning and Development shall review these items for
compliance with all current applicable regulations related to government access
telecast (and internet) and, in the event any item is found to be in violation
of same, shall notify the party submitting same of the nature of the violation
with reference to the applicable regulation.
(Ord. 10-O-80. Passed 9-7-10; Ord. 18-O-075. Passed 9-4-18.)
155.27 DECISION.
   In such matters where the Municipal Planning Commission may be required by
law to state findings of fact and conclusions of law in support of its decision
and, if the applicant or other party requests such findings of fact and
conclusions of law, the request shall be made prior to or immediately after the
Commission's vote on the matter. The Chairman may request all parties submit
proposed findings of fact and conclusions of law and establish a deadline for
their submission to the Commission.
   The Commission shall have a reasonable time within which to prepare said
findings of fact and conclusions of law and to adopt same as part of its
decision and record of the case.
   In the event findings of fact and conclusions of law are required of the
Municipal Planning Commission by any reviewing body, the Commission, on its own
motion, may proceed to adopt same in the same manner as provided herein above.
(Ord. 10-O-80. Passed 9-7-10.)
