Conflict of interest - see CHTR.
8.08
 
 
163.01 ESTABLISHMENT OF COMMISSION.
   There is established a City Beautification Commission consisting of eleven
(11) citizen members who shall serve without compensation and who shall be
appointed by Council for a term of four (4) years, except that the term of
three of the citizen members of the first commission shall be for a term of two
years, and the term of three citizen members shall be for a term of one year.
one of said citizen members shall be designated "Member for the Preservation of
Open Spaces." City Tree Commission members may also serve as members of the
City Beautification Commission. The Director of Parks, Recreation and Public
Lands and the Superintendent of Parks and Public Lands shall be ex-officio
members of the Commission without voting rights.
(1969 Code 33.30)
163.02 PURPOSE.
   The Beautification Commission shall plan and direct general landscaping,
clean-up, paint-up and fix-up campaigns within the City and shall do all things
necessary to enhance the physical and natural beauty of the City's structures
and terrain.
(1969 Code 33.31)
163.03 POWERS.
   The powers of the City Beautification Commission shall be those granted by
this section and those which may be hereafter passed by Council relating to the
City Beautification Commission. (1969 Code 33.32)
163.04 PROCEDURES.
   The City Beautification Commission shall adopt its own rules and regulations
including the manner of selection of a chairman and adopt its methods of
procedure except as may otherwise be provided by Council or the laws of Ohio.
All meetings of the City Beautification Commission shall be open to the public.
(1969 Code 33.33)
163.05 MASTER PLAN.
   The City Beautification Commission shall develop and administer, pursuant to
direction from Council, a Master City Beautification Plan, consistent with the
City of Mentor's Master Comprehensive Plan. (1969 Code 33.34)
163.06 SLOGAN.
   The slogan for the City Beautification Commission shall be "Keep Mentor
Clean and Green" and the slogan shall be promoted, displayed and utilized
whenever possible, in all commission activities. (1969 Code 33.35)
CHAPTER 165
Community Arts Commission
165.01    Establishment of Commission.
165.02   Purpose.
165.03    Authority.
165.04    Procedure.
 
CROSS REFERENCES
Authority to establish - see CHTR.
3.15
Procedure - see CHTR.
6.05
 
 
 
165.01 ESTABLISHMENT OF COMMISSION.
   There is hereby established a Community Arts Commission of the City of
Mentor which shall consist of not less than eleven (11) members who shall serve
without compensation for a term of three years, eight (8) of which members
shall at all times be electors of the City of Mentor.
   If practicable, consideration shall be given to the appointment of
representatives of the following organizations, to wit: the Mentor Exempted
Village School District; the Mentor Public Library; the Creative Artists
Association of Lake County; Lakeland Community College, Humanities Department;
the Mentor Chamber of Commerce; the Lake County Historical Society; and a
Mentor Homeowner Association.
   The Director of Parks, Recreation and Facilities shall be an ex-officio,
non-voting member of the Commission.
   Vacancies occurring otherwise than by expiration of term shall be for the
unexpired term and shall be filled in the same manner as original appointments.
(Ord. 09-0-119. Passed 12-1-09.)
165.02 PURPOSE.
   The Community Arts Commission shall plan and coordinate a community-wide
cultural program which will encourage and expand cultural activities and
enrichment opportunities throughout and into the community. The Commission
shall seek to:
    (1)    Provide a continuing series of cultural events and experiences which
make living in the community a source of pleasure and inspiration;
   (2)    Provide an active role in educating and motivating the citizens of
Mentor to the value of the cultural arts;
   (3)    Significantly increase community involvement and interest in cultural
activities;
   (4)    Coordinate all applicable community resources which would provide for
a direct positive impact on community cultural enrichment;
   (5)    Utilize the arts as tools to enhance ethnic, historic and social
traditions pertinent to the City; and
   (6)    Seek donations and other funding for cultural activities.
(1969 Code 33.81)
165.03 AUTHORITY.
   The Community Arts Commission shall serve as an advisory commission to the
City of Mentor and shall have those powers granted by this section and those
which may hereafter be passed by Council relating to the Community Arts
Commission. (1969 Code 33.82)
165.04 PROCEDURE.
   The members of the Commission shall select their own chairman and secretary
and such other officers as are necessary. The Commission shall adopt such by-
laws as it deems necessary for the conduct of its business and activities.
(1969 Code 33.83)
