553.09 CONSTRUCTION OF NEW RAILWAY TRACKS.
    (a)    No new railway tracks shall be constructed within the City of Mentor
over or across Reynolds Roads, Center Street, Hart Street, Maple Street,
Station Street, Patterson Drive, Hopkins Road, Heisley Road, or any other
street in the City of Mentor by any person, firm or corporation without first
obtaining the written approval of the City Manager and City Engineer.
(1969 Code 99.03)
   (b)    Whoever violates this section is guilty of a misdemeanor of the first
degree.
553.99 PENALTY.
   (EDITOR'S NOTE: See Section
501.99 for penalties applicable to any misdemeanor classification.)
