CHAPTER 907
Streets
907.01    Cleaning of streets during construction.
 
 
CROSS REFERENCES
      Barricades and warning lights - see GEN. OFF.
521.03
      Placing injurious material in streets - see TRAF.
311.01
      Subdivision Regulations standards - see P. & Z.
1115.03,
1117.02
 
 
 
907.01 CLEANING OF STREETS DURING CONSTRUCTION.
   (a)    During the construction or installation of any improvement to real
property, the contractor to whom the permit is issued shall at the end of each
working day, remove from the traveled portion of all City streets any debris,
mud or dirt generated by such construction or installation.
   (b)    Any person, firm or corporation who violates subsection (a) hereof
shall be guilty of a minor misdemeanor and subject to the penalties set forth
in Section
501.99 of the General Offenses Code. (1969 Code 97.02)
CHAPTER 913
Sidewalks
913.01   Definitions.
913.02    Notice to construct or repair sidewalks.
913.03    Service upon agent or owner.
913.04    Notice to non-residents and persons not found.
913.05    Sidewalks, curbing, and gutters in City.
913.06    Sidewalk maintenance.
913.07    Emergency repair.
913.08    Installation of driveway drain required.
913.09    Maintenance of yards and ditches.
913.10    Construction by City.
913.99    Penalty.
 
CROSS REFERENCES
       Construction and repair of sidewalks - see Ohio R.C. Ch. 729
      Sidewalk obstructions - see GEN. OFF.
521.04
      Duty to keep sidewalks in repair and clean - see GEN. OFF.
521.06
 
 
 
913.01 DEFINITIONS.
   Unless the context specifically indicates otherwise, the meanings of terms
used in this chapter shall be as follows:
   "Sidewalk" shall mean any Portland cement concrete walkway constructed in
that portion of the street right-of-way designed particularly for pedestrian
travel.
   "Director" shall mean the Director of Public Works of the City.
(1969 Code 97.05)
913.02 NOTICE TO CONSTRUCT OR REPAIR SIDEWALKS.
   When the Council declares by resolution that certain specified sidewalks,
curbing, or gutters shall be constructed or repaired, the Clerk of the Council
shall cause a written notice of the passage of such resolution to be served
upon the owner or agent of the owner of each parcel of land abutting any such
sidewalk who is a resident of the City, in the manner provided for the service
of summons in a civil action, and shall return a copy of such notice with the
time and manner of service endorsed thereon, to the Council, which shall file
and preserve it.
(1969 Code 97.10)
913.03 SERVICE UPON AGENT OR OWNER.
   For the purpose of the service under Section
913.02 if the owner is not a resident of the City, any person charged with the
collection of rents or the payment of taxes on the property, or having general
control thereof in any way, shall be regarded as the agent of the owner, and
the return shall have the same effect as the sheriff's return on summons in
civil action.
(1969 Code 97.11)
913.04 NOTICE TO NON-RESIDENTS AND PERSONS NOT FOUND.
   If it appears in any return under Sections
913.02 and
913.03, that the owner is a nonresident of the County, or that neither the
owner or agent or the place of residence could be found, publication of a copy
of the resolution once in a newspaper of general circulation in the City is
sufficient notice to such owner, but no publication of the resolution shall be
necessary in the case of construction or repair of sidewalks, curbing, and
gutters where the notice is served upon the owner or agent as provided in
Sections
913.02 and
913.03.
(1969 Code 97.12)
913.05 SIDEWALKS, CURBING AND GUTTERS IN CITY.
   If the sidewalks, curbing, or gutters mentioned in Section
913.02 are not constructed within 60 days, or not repaired within 30 days, from
the service of the notice or completion of the publication, the Council may
have such construction or repair done at the expense of the owner and report
the cost thereof to such owner. Such cost shall constitute a lien on the
property abutting on such sidewalks from the date it is so reported to the
owner, and shall be paid by him to the Director of Finance. If the cost is not
paid within 10 days from the time it was reported to such owner, the Director
of Finance shall certify it, with a forfeiture of 5 percent thereon, to the
County, who shall place it on the tax duplicate and collect such costs and
forfeitures in the same manner as other taxes are collected.
(1969 Code 97.14)
913.06 SIDEWALK MAINTENANCE.
   All sidewalks within the City shall be kept and maintained in good repair by
the owner of the land adjacent to and abutting upon the same; and if any owner
shall neglect to keep and maintain the sidewalk along the front, rear or side
of the land owned by him, in good repair and safe for the use of the public,
the said owner shall be liable to the City for any damages recovered against
the City sustained by any person by reason of said sidewalk being unsafe and
out of repair. (1969 Code 97.16)
913.07 EMERGENCY REPAIR.
   If the Director shall determine that the condition of any sidewalk is such
that immediate repair is necessary to protect the public, he shall immediately
proceed to repair the same without notice to the owner of the land abutting
thereon or adjacent thereto. The cost of such emergency repairs shall be
charged against the land which said sidewalk adjoins and the owner of said
land, and shall be collected as a single lot assessment.
(1969 Code 97.17)
913.08 INSTALLATION OF DRIVEWAY DRAIN REQUIRED.
   Each owner of any land, lot or premises abutting upon a street, road or
highway in the City, shall install and maintain a driveway drain or culvert in
condition so as to permit the free flow of road and surface water along said
street, road or highway. Said drain or culvert shall be not less than eight (8)
inches in diameter, or of such larger size as to permit the free passage of
water from the ditch from one end of said drain or culvert to the other end.
(1969 Code 97.20)
913.09 MAINTENANCE OF YARDS AND DITCHES.
   Every owner or occupant of any land, lot or premises abutting upon any
alley, road or highway shall maintain the area between the right-of-way line
and the building line within his lot side-lines in grass and trees, with at
least one tree for every lot and one additional tree for every 100 feet of lot
width. Said owner or occupant shall further keep the right-of-way, gutter,
drain or ditch adjacent to the alley, road or highway, and within his lot side-
lines free from weeds, rubbish and debris and in good repair and free from
nuisance and hazards, and all trees located within the untraveled portion of
such street, road, highway or alley shall be maintained so as not to create a
hazard to persons or property.
(1969 Code 97.21)
913.10 CONSTRUCTION BY CITY.
   Upon notice from the Manager, each such owner of land, lot or premises shall
install or repair such drain or culvert under said driveway, or to comply with
Sections
913.08 and
913.09, at such owner's expense, which drain or culvert shall be of such size
as is specified in the notice by said Manager. Upon failure of owner to comply
with said notice, said Manager may proceed with the construction or repair of
said drain or culvert, and recover the cost; or said Manager may certify the
cost to the Auditor of Lake County, Ohio, for collection as other taxes and
assessments. (1969 Code 97.22)
913.99 PENALTY.
   Any person, firm or corporation who violates any provision of this chapter
is guilty of a misdemeanor of the fourth degree. Each day of violation of any
section hereof shall be a separate offense.
CHAPTER 919
Tree Regulations
919.01    Regulations and definitions.
919.02    Trimming.
919.03    Permit.
919.99    Penalty.
 
 
CROSS REFERENCES
      Power to regulate shade trees and shrubbery - see Ohio R.C. 715.20
      Assessments for tree planting and maintenance - see Ohio R.C. 727.011
      Injury or destruction - see GEN. OFF.
 541.06
      Tree preservation - see BLDG. Ch.
1357 
 
 
 
919.01 REGULATIONS AND DEFINITIONS.
   (a)   (1)   No person shall plant a tree upon the area in public right-of-
way, parks, or other public areas without having first obtained a written
permit from the Director of Public Works, hereinafter referred to as Director.
      (2)   No person shall remove, destroy, or injure any tree, or to
authorize any person to do so, or to remove or tamper with any device placed
for the protection of any such tree, or to attach any rope, wire, chain, sign
or other device whatsoever to said tree, or to authorize or cause same to be
done except having first obtained a permit from the Director.
   (b)    The word "person" as used in this chapter shall include individuals,
corporations, groups or individuals, firms, associations, and their servants,
agents or employees.
      (c)    The word "tree" whenever used in this chapter shall mean any tree,
shrub, or other woody plant in or upon any public right-of-way, park, or other
public areas or that part of any tree, shrub or other woody plant that extends
within the lines of any public right-of-way, park, or other public area, in the
City.
   (d) The word "permit" shall mean a permit in writing as issued by the
Director of Public Works.
   (e) The word "Director" shall mean the Director of Public Works, or his
designee.
(Ord. 21-O-059. Passed 10-19-21.)
919.02 TRIMMING.
   All trees shall be kept trimmed so as not to create a hazard to public
safety with minimum applicable clearances as determined by the Director of
Public Works. All trees having branches projecting over a public right-of-way
shall be kept trimmed by the owner of such private property so that the lowest
branches shall have the minimum clearance specified by the Director. If the
owner of such property shall neglect or refuse to trim such trees upon being
notified in writing by the Director to do so, the Director may, after the
expiration of the date specified in said notice, cause such trimming to be done
at the expense of the owner based on actual cost to the City plus a twenty-five
percent (25%) field inspection fee thereon, shall be certified to the County
Auditor who shall enter said amount so certified on the tax duplicate as a
special charge against the real estate on which said tree is located and the
same shall be collected as other taxes, and when collected shall be paid to the
City.
(Ord. 18-O-026. Passed 7-3-18.)
919.03 PERMIT.
   (a)   The application for any permit required hereunder shall be made in
writing to the Director upon forms furnished by him and shall specify the
particular kind of work or operation the applicant desires to perform
thereunder and shall state the exact location and species of any tree or trees
affected. The permit shall be effective for such length of time as the Director
shall in each case determine, which shall be indicated on the permit, and such
permit may be revoked at any time at the discretion of the Director upon
finding that the terms and conditions upon which the permit has been issued are
or have been violated.
   (b)   No person shall interfere with such person or persons as are directed
by the Director to carry out the provisions of this chapter or who may be
directed to do any of the work ordered to be done hereunder.
      (c)    The Director of Public Works may issue a permit to remove or cut
down a tree when one of the following applies:
      (1)   The tree is damaged or diseased to an extent that it is unlikely to
survive or presents itself in such a diminished form so as to noticeably
misrepresent the species.
      (2)   Damage is inflicted to the root system by machinery, storage of
materials and/or soil compaction.
      (3)   The natural grade is changed above or below the root system or
around the trunk.
      (4)   Damage is inflicted on the tree that would permit fungus or pest
infection.
            (5)    The tree is excessively pruned or thinned.
            (6)    Areas are paved with concrete, asphalt or other impervious
material within such proximity to the tree as to be harmful to the tree.
            (7)    The tree species is nearing the end of its predictable age
and it is desirable to replace it with a younger tree.
            (8)    The tree has been placed in an area that, due to the size or
shape of the tree, or the size of the area where it is planted, it is unlikely
to remain healthy or is likely to cause significant damage to public
infrastructure.
            (9)    The Director deems, at his discretion, that a tree should be
removed.
      (d)    Subject to the additional requirements of this subsection, the
Director shall issue a permit for the removal of a tree which is defined in
Section
1162.02(A)(34) as an "undesirable tree."
      (1)    The tree shall be timely replaced within the planting season with
a species identified on the Master Street Planting List and as approved by the
Director in accordance with Administration guidelines, for including size,
species, and location appropriateness.
      (2)    The property owner shall be solely responsible for all expenses of
tree removal and replacement.
      (3)    The Director is authorized as a condition of permit approval to
obtain assurances that the property owner will comply with the permit
conditions, inclusive of contracts for removal and replacement as well as proof
of financial ability.
      (4)    No more than 15 total permits may be issued in any calendar year.
     (e)   The Director shall indicate that removal of a tree shall include the
entire tree and tree stump and may require the replacement of the tree as a
condition for approval.
(Ord. 22-O-072. Passed 10-4-22.)
919.99 PENALTY.
   Whoever violates subsections (a)(1) or (a)(2) of Section
919.01, Section
919.02, or subsection (b) of Section
919.03 is guilty of an unclassified misdemeanor and subject to a fine not to
exceed two thousand dollars ($2,000) and an order of restitution.
(Ord. 21-O-059. Passed 10-19-21.)
CHAPTER 925
Right of Way Construction Code
