925.12    Review and approval.
925.13    Notice of denial.
925.14    Denial or revocation of permit; appeal.
925.15    Permit time limitations.
925.16    Inspections required.
925.17    Work started without a permit.
925.18    Required improvements.
925.19    Extraterritorial street connections.
925.20    Fees.
925.99    Penalty.
 
 
 
GENERAL PROVISIONS
 
925.01 PURPOSE AND INTENT.
   This chapter shall be known, cited and referred to as the "Mentor Right-of-
Way Construction Code".
   The purpose of this chapter is to provide controls and standards for
construction activities within or traffic impacts to the public rights-of-way
and within certain easements dedicated for public use, and to control additions
to the storm drainage system of the City, with the intent of safeguarding the
public interest in the facilities and benefits provided therein.
(1969 Code 155.11)
925.02 DEFINITIONS.
   For the purposes of this chapter, the following words and phrases shall have
the meanings respectively ascribed to them by this section.
    (a)    Boring - A construction method involving pushing, tunneling, or
drilling a pipe or cable under pavement.
   (b)    City Engineer - The City Engineer of the City of Mentor.
   (c)    Construction Plans - The maps, drawings, and specifications
accompanying an application or permit showing the specific location and design
of improvements to be installed.
   (d)    Curb or Pavement Cut - Cutting, removal, or other alteration of
existing pavement, curb or gutter.
   (e)    Public Easement - Authorization by a property owner for use by the
City and for a specified purpose, of any designated part of his property. This
definition does not include easements granted for utility services, pursuant to
a utility easement, as hereinafter defined.
   (f)    Registered Contractor - A contractor lawfully registered by the City
of Mentor as required by this chapter.
   (g)    Right-of-Way - Land occupied or intended to be occupied by a street,
crosswalk, walkway, or other public improvement relating to public travel,
access or use.
   (h)    Right-of-Way Improvement - Any physical improvement located within
the bounds of, on the surface of, above, or below a dedicated public street,
right-of- way, or easement, including, but not limited to streets, sidewalks,
curbs, gutters, driveway aprons, water lines, electric lines, sanitary sewer
lines, storm sewer lines, ditches, swales, culverts, drains, cable television
wires, and gas lines.
   (i)    Sidewalk - Any walkway constructed in that portion of a public right-
of-way or easement designed particularly for pedestrian travel.
   (j)    Storm Drainage Improvement - Any facility, including but not limited
to swales, ditches, pipes, and drains which collect, store, channel, direct, or
otherwise physically control surface or subsurface water and cause such water
to flow into the storm sewer system or other storm water control facility of
the City of Mentor. For the purposes of this chapter, the term "storm drainage
facility" shall include such facilities constructed on private property.
   (k)    Tree Lawn - The area of the right-of-way located between the street
pavement and the right-of-way line.
   (l)    Traffic Impact - Amount of delay time to traffic resulting from
development of land as determined by the Highway Capacity Manual, Special
Report 209, 3rd Edition, Washington, D.C.; Transportation Research Board 1994
and amendments or additions thereto.
   (m)    Trip Generation - Traffic resulting from development of land as
determined by Trip Generation, 5th Edition, Washington, D.C.; Institute of
Transportation Engineer and amendments or additions thereto.
    (n)    Utility Easement - Authorization by a property owner for the use of
a designated part of his property for the specific purpose of constructing,
placing, operating, maintaining, repairing, reconstructing or relocating
facilities related to the distribution and transmission of utility services
and/or any other communication entities franchised to serve the community, for
public and private use.
      (1969 Code 155.12)
REGISTRATION OF CONTRACTORS
925.03 REGISTRATION REQUIRED.
   No contractor shall perform any work in the City without first obtaining a
certificate of registration from the City Engineer. Any contractor who
contracts with the general public to perform work regulated by this chapter
must be registered with the City to do such work.
   "Contractor", as used within this chapter, means any individual, firm,
partnership, corporation, association or other organization, or any combination
thereof, who or which by himself, or itself, or by or through others,
constructs, alters, repairs, adds to, subtracts from, reconstructs or remodels
any right-of-way improvement, or storm drainage improvement, or who or which
undertakes or offers to undertake, or purports to have the capacity to
undertake, or submits a bid to do such work. The term "contractor" includes a
subcontractor and all specialty contractors whose operations as such are the
performance of construction work requiring skills, including, but not limited
to, plumbing, electrical, paving, landscaping, grading, drainage.
(1969 Code 155.21)
925.04 APPLICATION FOR CERTIFICATE OF REGISTRATION.
   (a)    Application for a certificate of registration shall be upon forms
provided by the City Engineer. The application shall include the name, current
address and telephone number of the contractor applying, and designate the form
of business organization, whether corporation, partnership, individual, or
other organization. When the applicant is other than an individual, he shall
state the name, address and telephone number of the individual charged with the
management of the work of the business organization to be performed within the
City. The application shall contain such other information as the City Engineer
deems pertinent.
   (b)    Applicants shall meet the following criteria:
      (1)     No applicant shall be eligible for registration under the
provisions of this chapter unless such applicant is:
         A.    At least eighteen (18) years of age;
         B.    Able to interpret construction drawings and specifications;
         C.    Able to comply with the requirements of this chapter.
      (2)    When an applicant for registration is a firm or corporation, each
responsible member of such firm or corporation, listed as such in the
application for registration, shall individually be qualified for registration
under the provisions of this chapter.
   (c)    It shall be the responsibility of each registered contractor to
immediately notify the City Engineer of any changes in the information provided
on his application form and of any change in status regarding the required bond
or liability insurance coverage.
(1969 Code 155.22)
925.05 ISSUANCE OF REGISTRATION CERTIFICATE.
   The City Engineer shall issue a certificate of registration to each
contractor applying when each of the following conditions have been met:
   (a)    A completed application form has been filed.
   (b)    The applicant has furnished and filed with the City Engineer, a bond
in the sum of ten thousand dollars ($10,000.00) to be approved by the Law
Director, guaranteeing full and faithful compliance with all provisions of the
Mentor Building and Zoning Codes.
   (c)    The applicant has tendered the certificate of registration fee as
specified in Section
925.20 .
   (d)    The applicant has furnished evidence of liability insurance for
bodily injury in the minimum amount of One Million Dollars ($1,000,000) and for
property damage in the minimum amount of One Million Dollars ($1,000,000) .
   (e)    The applicant has furnished evidence of having duly registered with
the Tax Division of the City of Mentor Finance Department, on forms provided by
the Finance Department.
   (f)   The applicant has paid the fees established in Section
925.20 .
   The certificate of registration authorized to be issued hereunder shall be
valid for the calendar year in which it is issued and shall be renewed on an
annual basis thereafter.
(Ord. 08-0-35. Passed 5-6-08.)
925.06 REVOCATION OF REGISTRATION.
   The City Engineer may refuse to issue or revoke any original or renewal
certificate of registration when, in his opinion, the certificate holder has
performed work in a careless or irregular manner resulting in repeated or
continuing violations of the ordinances and policies of the City or when the
City Engineer has evidence that the bond required is no longer in effect. The
City of Mentor shall give notice of such revocation to the contractor by
certified mail directed to the contractor at the address appearing on the
current application, stating in detail the facts and conclusions upon which the
revocation is based. The notice shall also contain a copy of Section
925.07 setting forth appellate procedures from the order of revocation.
(Ord. 08-0-35. Passed 5-6-08.)
925.07 APPEALS.
   Any contractor whose application for registration or annual renewal of his
registration has been refused or whose registration has been revoked, may
appeal the refusal or revocation to the Board of Building and Zoning Appeals.
Such appeal shall be filed with the Department of Planning and Development on
forms provided for such purpose within ten days of the refusal of registration
or receipt of the notice of revocation. Upon receipt of the appeal, a hearing
shall be scheduled at the next regular meeting of the Board. Notice of the time
and place of the hearing shall be given to the contractor by first class mail
to the address appearing on the appeal form. At the hearing, the contractor
shall have the opportunity to present evidence and witnesses in support of his
appeal. Within a reasonable time after the hearing, the Board shall either
affirm, modify or reverse the decision of the City Engineer by a majority vote
of members present. Notice of said decision shall be sent to the contractor and
a copy filed with the contractor's registration file.
(Ord. 08-0-35. Passed 5-6-08; Ord. 18-O-075. Passed 9-4-18.)
925.08 PROPERTY OWNERS' EXEMPTION.
   The provisions requiring registration shall not apply to a homeowner
desiring to perform work regulated by this chapter so long as such work is
actually performed on land owned by, or under the maintenance responsibility of
the home owner and is actually performed by the homeowner. Any work performed
by the homeowner shall be subject to all other provisions of this chapter and
to all inspections and fees required under this chapter.
(Ord. 08-0-35. Passed 5-6-08.)
925.09 VIOLATIONS AND PENALTIES.
   Any false statement made and entered in to the permit application with the
purpose of circumventing the registration requirement is just cause for
revocation of the permit.
   Any person or contractor who performs or authorizes the performance of work
regulated by this chapter in the City without first obtaining a certificate of
registration shall be guilty of a fourth degree misdemeanor and shall be
subject to the penalties set forth in Section
501.99 of the General Offenses Code for fourth degree misdemeanors.
   Any person or contractor who performs or authorizes the performance of work
in the City after having his application for registration refused or after
having his certificate of registration revoked shall be guilty of a third
degree misdemeanor and shall be subject to the penalties set forth in Section
501.99 of the General offenses Code for third degree misdemeanors.
(Ord. 08-0-35. Passed 5-6-08.)
RIGHT-OF-WAY CONSTRUCTION PERMITS
925.10 PERMITS REQUIRED.
   Right-of-way construction permits shall be required prior to the start of
any work or the removal or disturbance of any soil in the public right-of-way
or in a public easement for the purpose of constructing, connecting,
disconnecting, repairing, removing, replacing, or altering
any improvement within the right-of-way, including but not limited to sidewalk,
pavement, curb, gutter, water line, storm sewer, electric line, sanitary sewer,
gas line, ditch, swale, culvert, drain, driveway apron, cable television line,
phone line or any other utility service connection or to significantly alter
the direction, volume, or velocity of surface or subsurface stormwater
drainage.    
   Stormwater construction permits shall also be required for the construction,
repair, replacement, removal or alteration of any storm drainage improvement in
the public right-of- way, in a public easement or on private property when
connected to a public stormwater improvement, including but not limited to
drains, catch basins, culverts, pipes, "french drains", "trench drains", or
other underground or in-ground structures or devices which collect, store,
channel, direct or otherwise physically control surface or subsurface water and
cause such water to flow into the stormwater system of the City of Mentor.
   The City Engineer shall establish policies, procedures, and standards for
the submission, review, and issuance of construction permits in a manner
compatible with the purposes of this chapter, provided, however, that pavement
cuts shall not be permitted without prior approval of the Council of the City
of Mentor unless the City Manager determines that there is an emergency
condition requiring immediate action.
(Ord. 08-0-35. Passed 5-6-08.)
925.11 APPLICATION FOR PERMIT.
   Requests for construction permits shall be made to the office of the City
Engineer together with such data as may be required to ensure compliance with
the purpose and intent of this chapter. (1969 Code 155.32)
925.12 REVIEW AND APPROVAL.
   Upon receipt of a request or a construction permit, the City Engineer shall
review such request together with all additional data submitted, for compliance
with this chapter and with the policies, procedures, and standards he shall
establish. Within a reasonable time, he shall either issue or deny the
construction permit requested.
(1969 Code 155.33)
   
925.13 NOTICE OF DENIAL.
   If, upon review of an application, the City Engineer finds such request or
data submitted with such request to be incomplete or otherwise unsatisfactory,
he shall issue to the applicant a written notice of denial containing the
reasons therefor.
(1969 Code 155.34)
925.14 DENIAL OR REVOCATION OF PERMIT; APPEAL.
   Permits issued pursuant to this chapter may be revoked at any time by the
City Engineer for good cause.
   Within three (3) working days of the revocation of a permit, the City
Engineer shall send notice to the person whose permit was revoked, setting
forth specifically the grounds of the revocation. Such notice shall be mailed
to the person to whom the permit was issued at the address shown on the permit
application.
   Any person aggrieved by a decision of the City Engineer in regard to the
denial or revocation of a permit shall have the right to appeal to the Board of
Building and Zoning Appeals. Such appeal shall be submitted and heard according
to the rules and procedures of the Board.
   Such appeal must be filed within ten (10) days of receipt of the written
verification of such denial or revocation.
(1969 Code 155.35)
925.15 PERMIT TIME LIMITATIONS.
   Any permit issued shall become invalid unless the work authorized by it
shall have been commenced within sixty (60) days after its issuance or if the
work authorized by such permit is suspended or abandoned for a period of six
(6) weeks after the time the work is commenced; provided that, for cause, one
or more extensions of time for periods not exceeding sixty (60) days each may
be allowed in writing by the City Engineer.
(1969 Code 155.36)
925.16 INSPECTIONS REQUIRED.
   Inspections of work performed under construction permits will be made by the
City Engineer or his duly authorized representatives at such times and in such
manner as may be designated on such construction permits or as established in
the written policies or procedures of the Department of Engineering. Notice
shall be given to the Department of Engineering at least 24 hours prior to the
start of any work for the purpose of scheduling inspections. Fees for
inspections shall be charged as established in Section
925.20.
(1969 Code 155.37)
925.17 WORK STARTED WITHOUT A PERMIT.
   The fees required by Section
925.20 shall be doubled for work, for which a permit is required by this code,
started prior to obtaining a permit. An additional late charge of 10% (ten
percent) shall be added onto the cost of all permit fees for work which has
been started without a permit, for each month or fraction thereof, such permit
is not obtained after first being notified to stop work or obtain the proper
permit.
   Exception: Emergency repairs shall not be cause for late fees where the work
is performed by a registered contractor and the City is notified as soon as
possible during normal working hours and the permits are applied for and
obtained in a timely manner.
(Ord. 08-0-35. Passed 5-6-08.)
925.18 REQUIRED IMPROVEMENTS.
   Any person, firm, corporation, owner or lessee of any lot or land,
constructing or causing to construct access to any public roadway in the City,
except from residential subdivisions totaling less than five (5) acres, shall
first present to the City the results of a trip generation study and a traffic
impact study performed by an engineer qualified and pre- approved by the City
Engineer. The trip generation and the traffic impact study shall describe the
maximum anticipated traffic volumes by location and direction to be generated
and which will impact the road system during a peak design hour in the year of
construction plus twenty (20) years. The report shall also provide the means to
compensate for any degradation of the traffic services existing on the City
roadway system, to the City Engineer's satisfaction prior to the granting of a
permit for construction. Improvements to the City roadway system shall be
constructed as part of the development and its permit and the developer shall
provide inspection fees, a testing deposit and as surety representing 100% of
the cost of improvements.
(Ord. 08-0-35. Passed 5-6-08.)
925.19 EXTRATERRITORIAL STREET CONNECTIONS.
    No right-of-way improvement shall connect with a street or road in an
adjacent community except upon passage of an ordinance by Mentor City Council
authorizing a right- of-way improvement to connect with a street or roadway in
an adjacent community, and provided further, that such improvement is made in
compliance with the Right-of-Way Construction Code and in accordance with such
other conditions as the Council may provide.
(Ord. 08-0-35. Passed 5-6-08.)
925.20 FEES.
   The fees and deposits prescribed herein shall be additive and unless
otherwise specifically provided, shall be paid for each item listed.
   (a)    A fee of Seventy Dollars ($70.00) (Effective January 1, 2009 $100.00)
is hereby established for the original application for a certificate of
registration. A fee of Thirty-five Dollars ($35.00) (Effective January 1, 2009
$50.00) is hereby established for each annual renewal of a certificate of
registration within 30 days from the prior calendar year. The registration fee
after January 3l, shall be charged at the original application amount above.
   (b)   Storm water construction permit -$40.00 (Effective January 1, 2009
$50.00) which includes the first 100 lineal feet of storm drainage improvement,
or fraction thereof, plus $10.00 (Effective January 1, 2009 $20.00) for each
additional 100 lineal feet of storm drainage improvement or fraction thereof.
   (c)    Right-of-way Construction Permits - $40.00( Effective January 1, 2009
$50.00).
   (d)    Pavement open cut permit fee- $100.00 (Effective January 1, 2009
$200.00). In lieu of the fee, utility service providers shall be billed for
actual inspection and plan review time.
   (e)    Inspection and Plan Review charges including but not limited to
utility work, such as mains, trunks and transmission lines,$30.00/hour
(Effective January 1, 2009 $40.00/hour).
   (f)    Inspection charges necessary as a result of faulty construction, or
inadequate erosion and sediment control measures or inaccurate information,
given the Engineering Division $20.00/ inspection (to be deducted from
deposit).
   (g)   Prior to the issuance of any construction permit a construction
deposit shall be posted in the amount of $45.00 ( Effective January 1, 2009
$60.00). In the case of utility service providers, the City Engineer may waive
this deposit if a monthly billing process has been established.
   (h)    Inspection Deposits shall be required where the scope of work
dictates and where required to insure payment of inspection fees. The amount of
the inspection deposit shall be determined by the City Engineer.
      (Ord. 08-0-35. Passed 5-6-08.)
925.99 PENALTY.
    Any person or contractor who performs or authorizes the performance of work
regulated by this chapter without first obtaining the required certificate of
registration and permits shall be guilty of a fourth degree misdemeanor and
shall be subject to the penalties set forth in Section
501.99 of the General Offenses Code for fourth degree misdemeanors.
   Any person or contractor who performs or authorizes the performance of work
regulated by this chapter after having his application for registration refused
or after having his certificate of registration revoked shall be guilty of a
third degree misdemeanor and shall be subject to the penalties as set forth in
Section
501.99 of the General offenses Code for third degree misdemeanors.
(1969 Code 155.9)
